						 <hr /> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <td>Please <strong>do not</strong> message me (MaliceAforethought) asking me to add task forces to this list. Also do not send messages asking me to edit this list, or asking for the creation of new task forces. You can do that yourself. You have always been able to do that yourself. I don't know who keeps telling you to message me. Please stop. I have a family.</td> </tr> </table> <hr /> <p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> If this document confuses and scares you, and you don't understand what it is, read <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">this guide</a> until you feel better.</p> <p>The following list is <em>not</em> to be considered a canonical record of Mobile Task Forces within the Foundation universe. It is intended as a tool for writers, and is not considered 'official' by any stretch of the imagination.</p> <p>If you spot an MTF that's not on this list, or create a new one for your own SCP article or tale, feel free to insert it<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-326889-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>. If the number is already taken, just add a new entry below the original. Likewise, if you spot an MTF in this list that's no longer in existence, or goes by a different name/number, feel free to delete/edit it! This is primarily a collaborative project, so any additional help would be greatly appreciated. The formatting for adding a new item to the list is as follows:</p> <blockquote> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><tt><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">||&#32;MTF&#32;number</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-326889-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;||&#32;Codename/alias&#32;||&#32;Works&#32;it's&#32;used&#32;in</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-326889-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >3</a></sup><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;||&#32;Brief&#32;description&#32;of&#32;its&#32;purpose,&#32;goals,&#32;and&#32;current&#32;situation</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-326889-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >4</a></sup><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;||</span></tt></strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Entries marked with a '•' have been fully verified, and are confirmed to be accurate and up-to-date (or rather, as up-to-date as I can manage). Other stuff should be fine as well, but make sure to check first, and please don't verify your own entries!</p> <hr /> <h2><span>LIST OF TYPES OF TASK FORCES:</span></h2> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▷&nbsp;Show&nbsp;list</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">◁&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;list</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Type</th> <th>Abbreviation</th> <th>Details</th> <th>Example</th> </tr> <tr> <td>Mobile Task Force</td> <td>MTF</td> <td>The standard designation, any team of people that moves from place to place can technically be given the title MTF.</td> <td>MTF Alpha-1 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/tanhony-s-proposal">Red Right Hand</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Stationary Task Force</td> <td>STF</td> <td>What's that? Your team doesn't move? Use an STF name instead &#8212; if they're sitting in offices managing things, a Stationary Task Force sounds right up your alley.</td> <td>STF Beta-8 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3490">Bubble Blowers</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Naval Task Force</td> <td>NTF</td> <td>If your team mucks about on the ocean blue, chances are they're a Naval Task Force.</td> <td>NTF Delta-7 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3700">Northern Storm</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Provisional Task Force</td> <td>PTF</td> <td>Any task force formed to counter a single threat or incident. If they're only going to be used one time, Provisional is what you're looking for.</td> <td>PTF Duplic-4 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4029">Inner Workings</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Research Task Force</td> <td>RTF</td> <td>More boffins than brawlers, a Research Task Force specialises in investigating either a single anomaly, suspected anomaly, or type of anomaly. As with NTF and PTF, they can be used interchangeably with MTF.</td> <td>RTF Sigel-9 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3676">Oregon Trailblazers</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Special Task Force</td> <td>STF</td> <td>An esoteric, particular, or otherwise abnormal task force. Beyond that, what they are is up to you.</td> <td>STF-Omega-15 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2487">Dire Deeds</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Orbital Task Force</td> <td>OTF</td> <td>A task force. In space! If it's involved in orbits or space-stations, it's an OTF.</td> <td>OTF ग-3 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/first55">Cochrane's Children</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Joint Task Force</td> <td>JTF</td> <td>When the Foundation forms a group with members of other organisations, a JTF is what they make.</td> <td>JTF Delta-3 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-blackbird-and-the-falcon">Organic Free Trade</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Distributed Task Force</td> <td>DTF</td> <td>Multiple divisions, big or small, grouped under a single banner. This is the designation for you if they're tackling many things at once.</td> <td>DTF Sigma-6 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-120">Puddlejumpers</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Task Force</td> <td>TF</td> <td>All-encompassing designation for all types of Task Force. If you're not sure, just use this.</td> <td>TF-Theta-8 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2791">Invisible Hand</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Applied Task Force</td> <td>ATF</td> <td>Somewhat a hybrid between a provisional and stationary task force. Created for the purpose of containing a single anomaly, but not temporary. Don't travel and aren't ever reassigned.</td> <td>ATF Indianapolis-13 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/djkaktus-s-proposal-ii">Killboys&quot;</a>)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Collaborative Task Force</td> <td>CTF</td> <td>A task force that works directly in conjunction with other task forces or GoIs.</td> <td>CTF-Psi-12 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2906">Madvillainy</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Cryptography Task Force</td> <td>CTF</td> <td>A task force designed to keep communication secure or tracking the output of information.</td> <td>CTF-4753-06 [<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4753">DATA MISSING</a>]</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Oceanic Task Force</td> <td>OTF</td> <td>Like Naval Task Forces, Oceanic Task Forces deal with activities on the sea.</td> <td>OTF Delta-7 (&quot;<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4778">Bay-Watchers</a>&quot;)</td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> <hr /> <h2><span>LIST OF LISTS OF TASK FORCES:</span></h2> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▷&nbsp;Show&nbsp;list&nbsp;for&nbsp;'Alpha'</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">◁&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;list</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Task Force</th> <th>Codename</th> <th>Pages used</th> <th>Operational Scope</th> </tr> <tr> <td>• <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#alpha-1">MTF-Alpha-1</a></td> <td>Red Right Hand</td> <td>See <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">this page</a> for information about this particular task force.</td> <td>A task force that reports directly to the O5 Council.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-2</td> <td>Resort Staff</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2421">SCP-2421</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force, tasked with maintaining SCP-2421's feeding areas (presented as a chain of resorts branded as &quot;Fundamental Springs&quot;).</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-2</td> <td>The Mailmen</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/agent-klein-s-personnel-file">Agent Klein's Personnel File</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/circeus-personnel-file">Agent Andrew C. &quot;Circeus&quot; Hunter's Personnel File</a></td> <td>Task force specialising in the transportation of low-risk anomalous items.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-2</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-691">SCP-691</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/skies-made-strange-hub">Skies Made Strange Hub</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-3</td> <td>Running Mates</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2078">SCP-2078</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force, commissioned in order to contain SCP-2078. No more than 49% of MTF Alpha-3 members possess American citizenship.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-3</td> <td>Made Whole</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4524">SCP-4524</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-3</td> <td>Lokie’s Lollygaggers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/letter-of-the-day">Letter of the Day</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-3</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3333">SCP-3333</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#alpha-4">MTF-Alpha-4</a></td> <td>Pony Express</td> <td>See <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">this page</a> for information about this particular task force.</td> <td>A task force that specialises in package delivery and postal services.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-4</td> <td>No Borders</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/djkaktus-s-proposal">SCP-001 - CODE NAME: djkaktus - The Children</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-5</td> <td>Honor Guard</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2490">SCP-2490</a></td> <td>Presumed to covertly track, monitor, and if necessary subdue persons who may be under the influence of anomalous effects.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-5</td> <td>Paranaughts</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3608">SCP-3608</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4200">SCP-4200</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force, tasked with leading exploration missions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-5</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4029">SCP-4029</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-6</td> <td>Game Changers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4978">SCP-4978</a></td> <td>A Mobile task force specializing in anomalous sports and physical contests.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-6</td> <td>Sam Micheals</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3059">SCP-3059</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-7</td> <td>Security Blanket</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2247">SCP-2247</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/how-dr-clef-saved-christmas">How Dr. Clef Saved Christmas</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-7</td> <td>Literature Professors</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4635">SCP-4635</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-8</td> <td>Ice Breakers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1350">SCP-1350</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#alpha-9">MTF-Alpha-9</a></td> <td>Last Hope, Party Poopers</td> <td>See <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">this page</a> for information about this particular task force.</td> <td>The reborn MTF-Omega-7. A Mobile Task Force explicitly intended to train and utilize humanoid SCP objects in the field.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CTF-Alpha-9</td> <td>Curious Cats</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4473">SCP-4473</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-10</td> <td>Extraordinary Evidence</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4519">SCP-4519</a></td> <td>A combat force assembled to carry out counteroffensive measures against <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/non-prophet-organization-hub">SAPPHIRE</a>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-10</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4711">SCP-4711</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-12</td> <td>Flatheads</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1650">SCP-1650</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-13</td> <td>Meat Packers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2445">SCP-2445</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-13</td> <td>Odor Eaters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4032">SCP-4032</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• STF-Alpha-15</td> <td>Catch &amp; Release</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4664">SCP-4664</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-16</td> <td>Uncle Mike's</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/internal-memo-regarding-a-theft">Interlude: An Internal Memo Regarding a Theft</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-17</td> <td>God’s Pallbearers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2612">SCP-2612</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-19</td> <td>Romeo and Juliets</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2776">SCP-2776</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-19</td> <td>Alt-Fight</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3210">SCP-3210</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-20</td> <td>Holy Divers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1730">SCP-1730</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-21</td> <td>Julia's Angels</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3023">SCP-3023</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-21</td> <td>DDT Did Nothing Wrong</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3428">SCP-3428</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-23</td> <td>Meddling Earthlings</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3551">SCP-3551</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-26</td> <td>Devour Dawn</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2596">SCP-2596</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-27</td> <td>MTF Who Demands Tows</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4601">SCP-4601</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-29</td> <td>Discovery Hunters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2716">SCP-2716</a></td> <td>A task force equipped to retrieve and re-contain objects on the lunar surface.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-30</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2776">SCP-2776</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-43</td> <td>Witch Hunters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5382">SCP-5382</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-44</td> <td>Big Game Hunters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2254">SCP-2254</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-45</td> <td>Janitors</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5092">SCP-5092</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5083">SCP-5083</a></td> <td>Specializes in conducting cleanup and repair following destructive missions by other Task Forces.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Alpha-67</td> <td>Weed Whackers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4032">SCP-4032</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Alpha-77</td> <td>Crux