wn powerful reality altering entities or similar threats. Headquartered in <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3480">Area-13</a>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-14</td> <td>Perfect Ten</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4262">SCP-4262</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force composed of agents from both the Foundation and the Global Occult Coalition specialized in extranormal combat scenarios. Tasked with terminating instances of SCP-4262-α and ensuring successful ELEIA events. Agents masquerade as Olympic Gold Medalists when not in combat.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Omega-15</td> <td>Bag and Tag</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4758">SCP-4758</a></td> <td>Locating and terminating SCP-4758-1 instances.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>STF-Omega-15</td> <td>Dire Deeds</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2487">SCP-2487</a></td> <td>SCP-specific Special Task Force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-16</td> <td>Grail Knights</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/operation-galahad">Operation Galahad</a></td> <td>Elite unit hand picked to explore the extra-dimensional realm Corbenic, and SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• TF-Omega-16</td> <td>The Contestants</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1456">SCP-1456</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force, currently operating a call-centre.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Omega-17</td> <td>Florida Men</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/finding-scalpel">Finding A Scalpel</a></td> <td>Stationed at a site near Miami, primarily for deployment in response to anomalous incidents occuring in the Everglades.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-18</td> <td>Patriots</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4661">SCP-4661</a></td> <td>Military task force embedded within the US armed forces.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-19</td> <td>Kids See Ghosts</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3651">SCP-3651</a></td> <td>Tasked with leading civilians to shelter and observing the phenomenon during an SCP-3651 event.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Omega-19</td> <td>Double Feature</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2677">SCP-2677</a></td> <td>Immediate short-term replacement of compromised personnel.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-20</td> <td>Thought Police</td> <td><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/koska-i-mysi">The Cat and The Mouse</a>, <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/fox-hunt">Fox Hunt</a></td> <td>Consists of two groups of operatives: the WOLFs (Psychics) and the LANCEs (Non psychics). Specialized in detainment of Persons-Of-Interest.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>STF-Omega-21</td> <td>Arcane Enforcers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4684">SCP-4684</a></td> <td>SCP-specific Special Task Force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-23</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2069">SCP-2069</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2141">SCP-2141</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-27</td> <td>Bad Deer Hunting</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/letters-to-a-prophet-2-scry-harder">Letters to a Prophet #2: Scry Harder</a></td> <td>MTF tasked with investigating Saturn Deer.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-31</td> <td>Sticky Fingers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4241">SCP-4241</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4363">SCP-4363</a></td> <td>Task force focused on seizing anomalous items and inanimate SCP-objects.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-33</td> <td>Ocean's Three-hundred</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4661">SCP-4661</a></td> <td>Temporary task force for recontaining Las Vegas.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-34-01</td> <td>Office Duty</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2205">SCP-2205</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-34-02</td> <td>Recon Unit</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2205">SCP-2205</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Omega-44</td> <td>Death Seekers</td> <td><a href="http://www.s